Yeah, actually.

262
00:11:26,227 --> 00:11:27,895
So, you read a file
that you liked,

263
00:11:27,937 --> 00:11:30,315
and then you gave the
agency the serial number,

264
00:11:30,357 --> 00:11:31,399
and they contacted us?

265
00:11:31,441 --> 00:11:33,860
Yes, our system insures
total anonymity.

266
00:11:33,901 --> 00:11:35,362
We're very proud of it.

267
00:11:35,403 --> 00:11:37,696
You should be.

268
00:11:37,738 --> 00:11:41,700
You're really
on top of stuff.

269
00:11:41,742 --> 00:11:43,077
Well, then if there's
nothing else,

270
00:11:43,119 --> 00:11:44,829
then the two of us
should talk.

271
00:11:44,871 --> 00:11:46,705
I actually...

272
00:11:46,747 --> 00:11:48,249
I don't think
we have to.

273
00:11:48,291 --> 00:11:49,250
You don't?

274
00:11:49,292 --> 00:11:50,669
Yeah, when I read
about you two

275
00:11:50,709 --> 00:11:52,212
I was pretty sure
I wanted you.

276
00:11:52,253 --> 00:11:54,881
But I just thought
we should meet
face to face.

277
00:11:54,922 --> 00:11:57,676
I've made my decision.

278
00:11:57,716 --> 00:11:59,469
I choose them.

279
00:11:59,511 --> 00:12:02,222
Oh, my God, this is great.

280
00:12:02,263 --> 00:12:04,224
This is so great.
Did you hear that?

281
00:12:04,265 --> 00:12:05,933
Yeah. I did.

282
00:12:07,519 --> 00:12:10,522
Thank you.
Thank you so much.

283
00:12:12,773 --> 00:12:14,859
You are so going to heaven!

284
00:12:21,074 --> 00:12:22,867
We got some really
great stuff.

285
00:12:22,909 --> 00:12:26,621
Yeah. Yeah, but I'm
not sure about some
of the bras I got.

286
00:12:26,663 --> 00:12:29,832
Oh, really? Do you want to try
some of them on for me?

287
00:12:29,874 --> 00:12:31,334
Oh, okay.

288
00:12:31,376 --> 00:12:34,379
Wait, are we in
Joey's imagination?

289
00:12:35,796 --> 00:12:37,591
Oh, no.

290
00:12:37,632 --> 00:12:39,926
I took one of Ross' bags
by mistake.

291
00:12:39,967 --> 00:12:41,844
And one of mine is missing.

292
00:12:41,886 --> 00:12:43,054
Oh, well, Ross probably
has it.

293
00:12:43,096 --> 00:12:44,472
You can get it
from him later.

294
00:12:49,936 --> 00:12:53,565
So... what do you think?

295
00:12:55,275 --> 00:12:58,695
I think we're not wearing
the same shirt anymore.

296
00:12:59,571 --> 00:13:01,948
Yeah. Yeah, Rachel
picked it out for me.

297
00:13:01,989 --> 00:13:03,283
She told me to trust her,

298
00:13:03,324 --> 00:13:05,201
and you know what,
I'm glad I did.

299
00:13:05,243 --> 00:13:08,162
I turned quite a few heads
on my way over here.

300
00:13:09,748 --> 00:13:13,293
Dude, I really don't think
you should be wearing that.

301
00:13:13,334 --> 00:13:15,503
Oh, I see.

302
00:13:15,545 --> 00:13:19,674
Somebody's afraid of little
competition with the ladies?

303
00:13:19,716 --> 00:13:23,177
Looks like someone
is the ladies.

304
00:13:23,219 --> 00:13:26,640
You're just jealous
because you couldn't
pull this off.

305
00:13:26,681 --> 00:13:30,851
Yeah. Now if you'll
excuse me, I have a date.

306
00:13:32,729 --> 00:13:36,023
See, all eyes on me.

307
00:13:41,696 --> 00:13:43,698
We are not
signing those papers.

308
00:13:43,740 --> 00:13:44,991
Why not?

309
00:13:45,032 --> 00:13:45,992
It's wrong.

310
00:13:46,033 --> 00:13:47,034
They made a mistake.

311
00:13:47,076 --> 00:13:48,827
They think we're somebody else.

312
00:13:48,869 --> 00:13:51,581
God works in mysterious ways.

313
00:13:51,623 --> 00:13:54,542
You have got to stop.

314
00:13:54,584 --> 00:13:56,461
But she liked us.

315
00:13:56,503 --> 00:13:59,464
She likes Dr. Chandler
and Reverend Monica.

316
00:13:59,506 --> 00:14:03,635
If you think about it,
I'm kind of like a reverend.

317
00:14:03,677 --> 00:14:05,512
I mean, as a chef,

318
00:14:05,553 --> 00:14:10,809
I serve God by feeding
the hungry and poor.

319
00:14:10,849 --> 00:14:13,852
Your veal chop is $34.95.

320
00:14:13,894 --> 00:14:17,190
Come on, Chandler, I think we've
been given an opportunity.

321
00:14:17,231 --> 00:14:19,066
The mistake has
already been made.

322
00:14:19,108 --> 00:14:21,194
They're writing up the papers
right now.

323
00:14:21,235 --> 00:14:23,363
But we're not the one
she chose.

324
00:14:23,404 --> 00:14:25,699
How can you feel
okay about this?

325
00:14:25,740 --> 00:14:29,076
Because...

326
00:14:29,118 --> 00:14:32,747
We may not be who
she thinks we are,

327
00:14:32,789 --> 00:14:35,625
but no one will ever love
that baby more than us.

328
00:14:35,667 --> 00:14:37,043
I know.

329
00:14:37,084 --> 00:14:38,837
I mean, who knows how long
it's going to take

330
00:14:38,877 --> 00:14:41,631
for someone else to give us
a baby?

331
00:14:41,673 --> 00:14:43,882
What if no one ever picks us?

332
00:14:43,924 --> 00:14:44,884
Oh, honey...

333
00:14:44,925 --> 00:14:46,927
Please.

334
00:14:46,969 --> 00:14:49,930
Please, we are so close.

335
00:14:51,766 --> 00:14:53,892
Monica, I want a baby, too,

336
00:14:53,934 --> 00:14:56,437
but this woman is giving away
her child.

337
00:14:56,479 --> 00:14:59,399
She deserves to know
who it's going to.

338
00:15:06,531 --> 00:15:09,116
Okay, you're right.

339
00:15:10,034 --> 00:15:14,205
So, we'll tell the truth,
and who knows,

340
00:15:14,247 --> 00:15:17,916
you know, maybe she'll
like us for us.

341
00:15:17,958 --> 00:15:20,545
Maybe she will.

342
00:15:21,629 --> 00:15:23,882
Why couldn't I have
been a reverend?

343
00:15:23,923 --> 00:15:26,467
You're Jewish.

344
00:15:26,509 --> 00:15:28,636
Technicality.

345
00:15:34,684 --> 00:15:36,728
Garden salad for the lady.

346
00:15:36,770 --> 00:15:38,479
Oh, that looks great.

347
00:15:38,521 --> 00:15:39,814
Good ordering.

348
00:15:39,856 --> 00:15:43,109
Seafood platter
for the gentleman,

349
00:15:43,150 --> 00:15:44,277
and extra fries.

350
00:15:44,318 --> 00:15:45,486
Enjoy.

351
00:15:48,489 --> 00:15:50,283
Mm, those fries look delicious.

352
00:15:50,324 --> 00:15:53,160
Oh, I didn't know
you liked French fries.

353
00:15:53,202 --> 00:15:56,038
Help yourself.
What's mine is yours.

354
00:16:00,167 --> 00:16:02,378
Oh, wow,
are those stuffed clams?

355
00:16:05,632 --> 00:16:09,469
Uh, yes they are
my stuffed clams.

356
00:16:11,512 --> 00:16:14,766
How about those fries,
though, huh?

357
00:16:14,808 --> 00:16:17,143
They're delicious.

358
00:16:21,188 --> 00:16:24,901
You are beautiful,
you know that?

359
00:16:24,943 --> 00:16:28,195
That is so sweet.

360
00:16:29,739 --> 00:16:32,116
Okay, yeah.

361
00:16:43,127 --> 00:16:45,922
Now look what you did!

362
00:16:45,964 --> 00:16:47,715
What is the matter with you?

363
00:16:47,757 --> 00:16:51,344
I don't like it when people
take food off of my plate, okay?

364
00:16:51,385 --> 00:16:53,680
But you just said
what's mine is yours.

365
00:16:53,721 --> 00:16:55,556
Well, I didn't mean it!

366
00:16:55,598 --> 00:16:58,810
Fine. Sorry.

367
00:16:58,852 --> 00:17:01,395
I didn't think it was
that big a deal.

368
00:17:02,856 --> 00:17:04,315
No, I'm sorry.

369
00:17:04,357 --> 00:17:06,860
I'm overreacting, okay?

370
00:17:06,901 --> 00:17:11,071
It's just... when it comes to
food I have certain rules, okay?

371
00:17:11,113 --> 00:17:12,866
I mean,

372
00:17:12,907 --> 00:17:17,370
there are things you do and, you
know, things that you don't do.

373
00:17:24,585 --> 00:17:26,212
Wow. This place looks great.

374
00:17:26,253 --> 00:17:28,381
Oh, you are going to love it.

375
00:17:28,422 --> 00:17:31,592
And I'm glad we're
finally doing this.

376
00:17:31,634 --> 00:17:32,886
Me, too.

377
00:17:32,927 --> 00:17:34,387
Here.

378
00:17:41,936 --> 00:17:44,230
So this was fun.

379
00:17:52,613 --> 00:17:55,449
Look, I really am sorry
about, you know, before,

380
00:17:55,491 --> 00:17:57,827
and I just want
to make sure you know

381
00:17:57,869 --> 00:17:59,286
that I really do like you.

382
00:17:59,328 --> 00:18:02,248
Sure. Just not as much as clams.

383
00:18:02,289 --> 00:18:04,458
Well, stuffed clams.

384
00:18:06,126 --> 00:18:08,254
Chocolate torte
for the lady.

385
00:18:08,295 --> 00:18:10,590
Cheesecake for the gentleman.

386
00:18:10,631 --> 00:18:12,132
Excuse me, sir.

387
00:18:12,174 --> 00:18:15,636
There seems to be some sort
of red crap on my cheesecake.

388
00:18:15,678 --> 00:18:18,723
Oh, yes, that's
a raspberry coulis.

389
00:18:18,765 --> 00:18:20,934
I'm so stupid
ordering cheesecake.

390
00:18:20,975 --> 00:18:23,937
Trying to be healthy.

391
00:18:23,978 --> 00:18:26,105
Oh, my God. Mm!

392
00:18:26,146 --> 00:18:28,858
All right, I'll just have
what she's having instead.

393
00:18:28,900 --> 00:18:31,110
Oh, I'm sorry, sir.
That was our last piece.

394
00:18:31,151 --> 00:18:34,030
Mm, mm.

395
00:18:34,072 --> 00:18:35,197
( beeping )

396
00:18:35,239 --> 00:18:36,323
Oh, no.

397
00:18:36,365 --> 00:18:37,450
This is work.

398
00:18:37,491 --> 00:18:38,952
I should call in.

399
00:18:38,993 --> 00:18:40,453
Can you excuse me?

400
00:18:40,494 --> 00:18:42,496
Oh, yeah, sure, no problem.

401
00:18:45,124 --> 00:18:46,292
What are you doing?

402
00:18:46,333 --> 00:18:48,544
I thought you don't share food.

403
00:18:48,586 --> 00:18:50,671
Sure I do.

404
00:18:50,713 --> 00:18:52,214
Coulis?

405
00:18:52,256 --> 00:18:53,800
No.

406
00:18:53,841 --> 00:18:56,803
If I can't have your clams,
you can't have my dessert.

407
00:18:56,844 --> 00:18:58,096
This is a two-way street.

408
00:18:58,137 --> 00:19:00,807
( chuckles )

409
00:19:00,848 --> 00:19:02,642
Really?

410
00:19:02,683 --> 00:19:04,518
Really.

411
00:19:04,560 --> 00:19:07,814
Now this all better
be here when I come back.

412
00:19:07,855 --> 00:19:09,065
Yeah, of course.

413
00:19:09,107 --> 00:19:10,942
I can control myself.

414
00:19:23,329 --> 00:19:25,665
Stop staring at me!

415
00:19:36,342 --> 00:19:39,386
Oh, just a tiny little...

416
00:19:42,890 --> 00:19:44,976
Uh-oh.

417
00:19:53,901 --> 00:19:56,612
I'm not even sorry.

418
00:19:59,073 --> 00:20:01,034
Hi.

419
00:20:01,075 --> 00:20:02,409
Hey.

420
00:20:02,451 --> 00:20:05,038
So these are
the preliminary forms

421
00:20:05,079 --> 00:20:06,539
for an open adoption.

422
00:20:06,580 --> 00:20:07,874
There's a lot
to go over,

423
00:20:07,915 --> 00:20:09,583
but I'll explain
everything as
we go through.

424
00:20:09,625 --> 00:20:13,838
Is that... is that
a picture?

425
00:20:13,880 --> 00:20:16,590
Yeah, it's a sonogram
they took of the baby last week.

426
00:20:16,632 --> 00:20:18,676
I thought you
might want to see it.

427
00:20:26,184 --> 00:20:28,019
Look, Doctor.

428
00:20:31,564 --> 00:20:33,566
Look, before we
sign anything,

429
00:20:33,607 --> 00:20:35,526
we really have to talk.

430
00:20:39,113 --> 00:20:40,823
We're not who
you think we are.

431
00:20:40,865 --> 00:20:41,866
I don't understand.

432
00:20:41,908 --> 00:20:44,077
The agency must have
made some mistake.

433
00:20:44,118 --> 00:20:45,786
My wife is
not a reverend,

434
00:20:45,828 --> 00:20:47,163
and I'm not a doctor.

435
00:20:47,205 --> 00:20:48,164
What?

436
00:20:48,206 --> 00:20:49,289
That's impossible.

437
00:20:49,331 --> 00:20:51,209
I could perform
an operation on you

438
00:20:51,250 --> 00:20:52,668
and prove it if you'd like.

439
00:20:52,710 --> 00:20:55,671
I have to check your file.

440
00:20:55,713 --> 00:20:57,757
Excuse me.

441
00:20:57,798 --> 00:20:59,008
So, who are you?

442
00:20:59,050 --> 00:21:01,802
Well, our names really are
Monica and Chandler.

443
00:21:01,844 --> 00:21:02,970
We're from New York.

444
00:21:03,012 --> 00:21:05,139
But the important thing
to know about us

445
00:21:05,181 --> 00:21:08,350
is how much we would care
for this little baby.

446
00:21:08,392 --> 00:21:10,477
So, you lied to me before?

447
00:21:10,519 --> 00:21:14,899
Well, we
"bore false witness."

448
00:21:14,941 --> 00:21:19,112
See? I could be
a reverend.

449
00:21:19,153 --> 00:21:20,696
I can't believe this.

450
00:21:20,738 --> 00:21:23,449
We were hoping that since
we told you the truth,

451
00:21:23,490 --> 00:21:24,992
that you still might
consider...

452
00:21:25,034 --> 00:21:26,326
Giving you my baby?

453
00:21:26,368 --> 00:21:29,122
You think I'd give you
my child after this?!

454
00:21:29,163 --> 00:21:30,497
You don't have to decide
right now.

455
00:21:30,539 --> 00:21:31,791
But if you could just
look at our file...

456
00:21:31,832 --> 00:21:33,167
I don't want to look
at your file!

457
00:21:33,209 --> 00:21:34,794
This is over.

458
00:21:39,215 --> 00:21:41,383
Erica, wait.

459
00:21:41,425 --> 00:21:43,761
I have nothing
to say to you.

460
00:21:43,803 --> 00:21:46,222
You have every reason
to be upset.

461
00:21:46,264 --> 00:21:47,473
We did lie,

462
00:21:47,514 --> 00:21:49,267
but only because
we've been waiting

463
00:21:49,308 --> 00:21:50,977
and trying to have baby
for so long.

464
00:21:51,018 --> 00:21:53,395
And we don't know how long
it's going to be

465
00:21:53,437 --> 00:21:55,355
before we get
another chance again.

466
00:21:55,397 --> 00:21:59,359
Why don't you ask the reverend
to pray on it.

467
00:21:59,401 --> 00:22:00,653
Erica, please.

468
00:22:00,694 --> 00:22:02,238
Just consider us.

469
00:22:02,280 --> 00:22:04,448
Ask them to see our file.

470
00:22:04,490 --> 00:22:06,366
Our last name's Bing.

471
00:22:06,408 --> 00:22:09,996
My wife's a chef
and I'm in advertising.

472
00:22:10,037 --> 00:22:12,665
Oh, yeah.

473
00:22:12,706 --> 00:22:16,085
I actually liked you guys.

474
00:22:16,127 --> 00:22:19,297
It doesn't matter,
because what you did was wrong.

475
00:22:19,338 --> 00:22:21,381
But you did like us.

476
00:22:21,423 --> 00:22:24,342
And you should.

477
00:22:24,384 --> 00:22:27,345
My wife's an incredible woman.

478
00:22:27,387 --> 00:22:30,850
She's loving and devoted
and caring.

479
00:22:30,891 --> 00:22:35,938
And don't tell her I said this,
but the woman's always right.

480
00:22:38,024 --> 00:22:43,112
I love my wife more than
anything in this world.

481
00:22:43,154 --> 00:22:50,161
And it... it kills me that
I can't give her a baby.

482
00:22:55,373 --> 00:22:58,585
I really want a kid.

483
00:22:58,627 --> 00:23:00,546
And when that day
finally comes,

484
00:23:00,587 --> 00:23:03,465
I'll learn how to be a good dad.

485
00:23:03,507 --> 00:23:05,509
But my wife...

486
00:23:05,551 --> 00:23:08,054
she's already there.

487
00:23:08,095 --> 00:23:10,931
She's a mother...

488
00:23:10,973 --> 00:23:13,684
without a baby.

489
00:23:18,772 --> 00:23:22,109
Please.

490
00:23:33,453 --> 00:23:36,123
You still want
that baby?

491
00:23:51,764 --> 00:23:53,974
God bless you,
Chandler Bing!

492
00:24:07,321 --> 00:24:10,574
Turns out this sweater is
made for a woman.

493
00:24:12,492 --> 00:24:14,620
So, why are you
still wearing it?

494
00:24:14,661 --> 00:24:16,663
Because it's soft.

495
00:24:18,374 --> 00:24:20,126
Hey, so how was your date?

496
00:24:20,167 --> 00:24:21,543
Not so good.

497
00:24:23,712 --> 00:24:25,089
Well, looks like

498
00:24:25,131 --> 00:24:29,260
it's just the two of us
tonight, huh, buddy?

499
00:24:29,302 --> 00:24:30,386
Yeah, and you know what?

500
00:24:30,428 --> 00:24:31,762
We could do a lot worse.

501
00:24:31,804 --> 00:24:32,805
Yeah.

502
00:24:32,846 --> 00:24:34,265
Yeah.

503
00:24:35,766 --> 00:24:38,685
Joey doesn't share food!

504
00:24:38,727 --> 00:24:42,189
Captioned by
Media Access Group at WGBH
access.wgbh.org

